s_workon_make cryptohome --test  Change-Id: Id8867fab4b1984c32186914dc0d413f59b3e6aca Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/472312 Commit-Ready: Ryo Hashimoto &lt;hashimoto@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ryo Hashimoto &lt;hashimoto@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="472312" owner_email="hashimoto@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/12/472312/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic506a5ce42c2b5d1feb4b202c981519b3a344db8" commit="d0a357ea9dc1fa5e33564c4d76769daf9aa61f83" commit_message="config_utils: support inherit keyword  Currently we have directory-based overriding for JSON config, so that we can have runtime overriding, and board specific overriding, using the same config name.  However, we also see another use case, where several configs would like to share a same base config file. For example, for Goofy plugins, we'd like to have a base setup for Chrome OS device, and make some tuning for different test lists.  Add this support in config_utils so that we can simply add 'inherit' in the top level JSON object:  {   &quot;inherit&quot;: &quot;&lt;base config name&gt;&quot;,   ... }  or  {   &quot;inherit&quot;: [&quot;&lt;base config name 1&gt;&quot;, &quot;&lt;base config name 2&gt;&quot;, ...],   ... }  After the directory-based overriding done, config_utils read the &quot;inherit&quot; field, load it, and override it with the current config.  BUG=None TEST=config_utils_unittest.py  Change-Id: Ic506a5ce42c2b5d1feb4b202c981519b3a344db8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/459258 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="459258" owner_email=